This is 99% invisible. I'm Roman Mars. They are hulking but graceful. Human-made whales that float in the air. For over 100 years lighter than air aircraft have fascinated us, and they have this recurring, storing role in our dreams of an alternate reality, of a future that might have been where cargo and passengers traverse the globe in a civilized fashion and dock elegantly on the morey towers on top of art that goes skyscrapers. If you've seen one in real life, it was likely a blimp emblazoned with the good year logo.
这里是 99% Invisible。我是罗曼·马斯。它们庞大而优雅。就像漂浮在空中的人造巨鲸。一个多世纪以来，轻于空气的飞行器一直让我们着迷，它们在我们对另一种现实、对未来的梦想中扮演着反复出现、历久弥新的角色：在那个未来里，货物和乘客以文明的方式穿梭于全球，并优雅地停靠在装饰派艺术摩天大楼顶部的系留塔上。如果你在现实生活中见过它们，那很可能是一艘印有固特异标志的软式飞艇。

