A blimp is a non-rigid airship, meaning there's no structure inside the balloon, it's just a balloon. The shape is maintained by the pressure of the lifting gas inside. Then you add a little cockpit and engines and rudders on the outside of that big balloon to make it fly. Today's blimps are basically cute PR novelties, but for around 100 years, lighter than air aircraft were seriously proposed as the perfect design solution for all kinds of problems, even though none of these proposals actually happened. People just couldn't give up on the promise of airships.
软式飞艇是一种非刚性飞艇，这意味着气囊内部没有任何结构，它就只是一个气囊。它的形状是通过内部升力气体的压力来维持的。然后，你在那个大气囊的外部加上一个小型驾驶舱、发动机和方向舵，让它飞起来。今天的软式飞艇基本上只是可爱的公关新奇玩意儿，但在大约100年的时间里，轻于空气的飞行器曾被认真地提议作为解决各种问题的完美设计方案，尽管这些提议最终都没有实现。人们就是无法放弃对飞艇的憧憬。

